WEBVTT

00:14:27.869 --> 00:14:30.329
is not about who can swap
lacrosse stories with you,

00:14:30.353 --> 00:14:32.712
or even who you're
excited to hang out with.

00:14:32.736 --> 00:14:35.326
Research suggests
that what you want is similarity

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.406
in core values,

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.101
values like flexibility,
or attention to detail.

00:14:41.517 --> 00:14:44.007
Sharing values tends
to promote team cohesion,

00:14:44.031 --> 00:14:45.872
coordination and commitment,

00:14:45.896 --> 00:14:48.437
which enhances performance and retention.

00:14:48.461 --> 00:14:50.123
LR: But what I was finding is

00:14:50.147 --> 00:14:52.805
that people were defining
cultural fit very differently.

00:14:52.829 --> 00:14:55.988
It turns out that one of the ways
that people measure cultural fit,

00:14:56.012 --> 00:14:58.493
either in a resume screen,
or in the job interview,

00:14:58.517 --> 00:15:00.533
was looking if they
had anything in common.